# Paths the `hygiene` guard's credential rule must not refuse.
#
# That rule matches on the path - `.env`, private keys, keystores, `.npmrc` - because the content
# scanner cannot help once a file is an opaque binary like a PKCS#12 store. Some credential-shaped
# paths hold no credential: an `.npmrc` setting `engine-strict`, a public certificate, a keystore
# used as a test fixture. Listing one here is the named way out, so that the first false positive is
# not met with `LEFTHOOK=0`, which turns off every other guard at the same time (ADR-0007).
#
# One path or glob per line, matched against the whole repository-relative path. `*` stops at a
# directory separator, `**` does not. A bare name is the path at the root, so listing `.npmrc` does
# not forgive `deploy/.npmrc`.
#
# This forgives the name only. `secrets` still scans the content, and the size and conflict-marker
# checks still apply - otherwise this file would be the way to smuggle a credential past the gate.
#
# Nothing needs allowing yet. Keep it that way where you can.
